    "name": "Orange Kabocha Squash",
    "description": "<p dir=\"ltr\"><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Flavor</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">: Sweeter than butternut squash, with a taste often described as a combination of sweet potato, pumpkin, and chestnuts.</span></p><ul class=\"lexical-text-editor--list-ul\"><li value=\"1\"><b><strong class=\"lexical-text-editor--bold\" style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">Texture</strong></b><span style=\"white-space: pre-wrap;\">: The cooked flesh is finely grained, dry, and fluffy. Its dense, creamy consistency holds its shape well, making it great for curries, stews, and roasting.</span></li></ul>",
